       •   When building with GCC 6 and link-time optimization (the --ffllttoo
           option to ggcccc), _C_o_n_f_i_g_u_r_e was treating all probed symbols as
           present on the system, regardless of whether they actually exist.
           This has been fixed.  [GH #15322]
           <https://github.com/Perl/perl5/issues/15322>

       •   _C_o_n_f_i_g_u_r_e now aborts if both "-Duselongdouble" and "-Dusequadmath"
           are requested.  [GH #14944]
           <https://github.com/Perl/perl5/issues/14944>

       •   Fixed a bug in which _C_o_n_f_i_g_u_r_e could append "-quadmath" to the
